         "slots": {
          "main": {
           "content": "{{Use mdy dates|date=May 2024}}\n{{Infobox NBA season\n| team           = Houston Rockets\n| misc           = \n| end_year       = 2025\n| wins           = 34\n| losses         = 21\n| division       = Southwest\n| division_place = 2\n| conf_place     = 4\n| playoffs       = \n| coach          = [[Ime Udoka]]\n| gm             = [[Rafael Stone]]\n| president      = Gretchen Sheirr\n| owner          = [[Tilman Fertitta]]\n| arena          = [[Toyota Center]]\n| television     = [[Space City Home Network]]\n| radio          = [[KBME (AM)|Sportstalk 790]]\n| bbr_team       = HOU\n}}\n\nThe '''2024–25 Houston Rockets season''' is the 58th season of the franchise in the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA), and 54th season in the city of [[Houston]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Houston Rockets Historical Statistics and All-Time Top Leaders |url=https://www.basketball-reference.com/teams/HOU/ |access-date=2023-05-01 |website=Basketball-Reference.com}}</ref> After starting the regular season out 3–3, the Rockets would start to showcase serious improvements in their production to the point of becoming one of the best teams in the Western Conference throughout the season.\n\n== Draft ==\n{{Main|2024 NBA draft}}\n{| class=\"wikitable sortable sortable\"\n! style=\"background:#c5001e; color:#fff; width:10%;\" |Round\n! style=\"background:#c5001e; color:#fff; width:10%;\" |Pick\n! style=\"background:#c5001e; color:#fff; width:20%;\" |Player\n! style=\"background:#c5001e; color:#fff; width:15%;\" |Position\n! style=\"background:#c5001e; color:#fff; width:15%;\" |Nationality\n! style=\"background:#c5001e; color:#fff; width:20%;\" |College / Club\n|- style=\"text-align: center\"\n|1\n|3\n|[[Reed Sheppard]]\n|[[Shooting guard|SG]]\n|{{flagicon|United States}} [[United States]]\n|[[2023-24 Kentucky Wildcats men's basketball team|Kentucky]]\n|- style=\"text-align: center\"\n|2\n|44\n|[[Pelle Larsson]]\n|[[Shooting guard|SG]]\n|{{flagicon|Sweden}} [[Sweden]]\n|[[2023-24 Arizona Wildcats men's basketball team|Arizona]]\n|}\n\nThe Rockets entered the draft (which was two days long instead of one day like it previously had been since the [[NBA draft]] was shortened down to two rounds in [[1989 NBA draft|1989]]) with a first-round pick and a second-round pick.<ref>{{cite web|title=2024 NBA Draft Order: Picks 1-58|url=https://www.nba.com/news/2024-nba-draft-order|website=NBA.com|date=May 14, 2024|access-date=May 30, 2024}}</ref>\n\n== Roster ==\n{{Houston Rockets roster}}\n\n==Standings==\n\n===Division===\n{{2024–25 NBA Southwest standings|team=HOU}}\n\n===Conference===\n{{2024–25 NBA West standings|team=HOU}}\n\n<!-- cassette: revision text cut here -->",
